  "lessons": "- **Indigenous & local community stories**: Consistently favored, especially First Nations advocacy, reconciliation, healing, land stewardship, and BC/Cariboo regional news. Local event coverage (e.g., community festivals) is accepted when it reflects real community life.\n- **Environmental & climate framing**: Accepted when the angle is solutions, protection, or scientific progress (sustainable farming, innovative climate action, EV market shifts, environmental policy stakes). Pure crisis, disaster, or lifestyle-trend framing is rejected.\n- **Science & nature discovery**: Favored for surprising natural phenomena, animal and evolutionary biology, astronomy, geoscience, space exploration, and medical or biological breakthroughs. Symptom-focused health advice and wellness pseudoscience are rejected.\n- **AI & tech: critical or substantive angles**: Accepted when covering security vulnerabilities, deployment or infrastructure significance, startup-ecosystem shifts with real impact, and nuanced concerns about trust, accountability, or labor. Promotional launches, hype, stock/funding drama, product comparisons, and speculative fiction are rejected.\n- **Privacy & security how-tos**: Practical guidance that empowers users (protecting accounts, spotting scams, tracking defenses) is valued. Product reviews, deals, and gadget optimization are not.\n- **Journalism & institutional accountability**: Valued for press freedom, government transparency, and corporate or legal accountability. Sensational crime, celebrity scandal, violent incidents, and tragedy-driven coverage are rejected.\n- **Local governance & civic life**: Favored for municipal and regional policy, public consultation, infrastructure, and community safety responses. Partisan election horse-race and national political spectac",
